# Participant data. Nothing under here may ever reach the remote: the raw
# college records, the nursing workbooks, and the SID-to-index linkage table
# are all directly or indirectly identifying.
data/
*.xlsx
*.xls
anonymised_records.csv
raw_college_records.*
*linkage*
*_linkage.csv

# The HMAC key that pseudonymises index numbers. Publishing it would make
# every pseudonym in every released table reversible by dictionary attack.
/local

# Ethics paperwork, consent forms, questionnaires, and the reference thesis
# collection. Third-party work and signed documents.
/proposal

# Generated artefacts. Every one is reproducible from the notebooks.
/results
*.pkl
*.docx

# Environments
ml_env/
venv/
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tooling
.gstack/

# NOTE: docs/ is deliberately NOT ignored here. The manuscript, the literature
# review and the topic document are the thesis and belong under version
# control. The predecessor repository ignored /docs/* wholesale, which meant
# moving these directories into docs/ removed them from git without warning.
# Every file under docs/ carries aggregate findings only: no record-level
# result, no identifier, no student name or index number appears in any of them.

# The *linkage* rule above keeps the SID-to-index table out of git. It also
# catches this analysis script by name. The script contains code, not data.
!notebooks/06_linkage_attack.py

# Downloaded source papers. Third-party copyright: reading copies are kept
# locally, the citations live in docs/literature/sources.md.
docs/literature/pdfs/

# Agent working notes. Local only, never published.
/AGENT.md
/HANDOFF_PROMPT.md
